# Obsidian vault

## Resolve the vault

Before read/write, resolve the vault root from (in order): the path the user
named this turn, a workspace folder that contains `.obsidian/`, or a connected
MCP that lists vaults. Do not guess a home-directory vault.

## Inventory

List or search notes under the resolved root. Prefer title + relative path.
Never invent note paths — search/list first. Skip `.obsidian/` internals unless
the user asked about app/settings/plugins config.

## Author / edit notes

- Body: Obsidian-flavored Markdown (headings, lists, callouts when the vault
  already uses them).
- Links inside the vault: `[[Note]]`, `[[Note#Heading]]`, `[[Note|alias]]`.
- Embeds: `![[Note]]` or `![[image.png]]`.
- Frontmatter: valid YAML between `---` fences; preserve unknown keys; do not
  invent Dataview / community-plugin fields unless already present in siblings.
- Prefer updating the existing note over creating a near-duplicate title.

Report the relative path written. Do not dump large private note bodies into
chat — quote only the changed excerpt when evidence is needed.
